    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0091" n="81" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg81"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Austria)/4–2145</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of the British Embassy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Makins</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Director of the Office of European Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Matthews</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-21">April 21, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Doc</hi>: With reference to our conversation
                    on April 19th about Austria, we have now heard from London that the Prime
                    Minister has decided, in the circumstances, not to send a message himself to
                    Stalin on this subject. Instead, instructions have been sent to His <pb
                        facs="0092" n="82" xml:id="pg82"/> Majesty’s Chargé d’Affaires in Moscow to
                    approach the Soviet Government through normal channels.</p>
                <p>2. I enclose a paraphrase of the instructions which have been issued to Mr. Frank
                        Roberts.<anchor n="60" xml:id="d58-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Yours ever,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roger Makins</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d58-a1.xml" xpointer="d58-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d58-f1" n="60" xml:id="d58-f1-content">
                <p>British Chargé in the Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
